# NextMoe developer portal (developer.nextmoe.dev) — frontend env example.
#
# Copy to `.env` and run `pnpm dev` (Nuxt dev server on :9430). The portal is a
# thin same-origin shell: the browser only ever talks to this app; Nitro proxies
# every /api/** call to the oauth service server-side (server/routes/api), so
# there is ZERO CORS and no backend change.
#
# NUXT_OAUTH_API_BASE is a SERVER-only var (never exposed to the browser). It is
# the base the /api/** relay forwards to — the path (e.g. /api/v1/dev/apps) is
# preserved. In production this is the docker service name; in local dev it is
# the locally-running oauth binary. Default (nuxt.config.ts) is the local oauth
# smoke port :19277.

# NUXT_OAUTH_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:19277   # local: `KUN_FIBER_SERVER_PORT=19277 go run ./cmd/oauth`
# NUXT_OAUTH_API_BASE=http://oauth:9277        # production (compose service name)
